    sourceFull: "Whole score (37 measures plus the first-ending bar), same Mutopia import as the opening above (bwv662.ly, Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0). The earlier 'broken at m26' import (111 ABC bars against 40) came from the source's \\slx helper, a hidden appoggiatura drawn only as a slur: the converter read each of its 32 uses as an extra real note, so the inner voices drifted out of their bars. The scratch copy converts to absolute pitches, drops the hidden appoggiatura (it is invisible in the engraving), and moves the alto's two-lane passage at bars 29-30 into its own voice; no sounding note changed. ly_abc_compare.py then found 0 differing bars across all voices (and every sounding note matches the original relative-pitch source), with no converter warnings. The repeat (bars 2-16, first and second endings) was set by hand. The left-hand staff stays in alto clef throughout (the source switches to treble in bars 5-9 and 17-19). The opening (bars 1-8) was re-derived from the same conversion: the 2026-08-15 draft was wrong in 7 of 8 bars. Checked against the .ly, not the engraved PDF (2026-10-02)."

