    fact: "One of the best-loved settings in the Orgelbüchlein, the collection of forty-five compact chorale preludes Bach assembled in Weimar as a teaching method for organists — an unbroken, gently florid melody floats over a steady walking bass, a miniature written around a Lutheran prayer for Christ's help \"in my last hour.\" Its hushed intensity later made it the recurring musical motif of Andrei Tarkovsky's 1972 film Solaris.",
